    "body": "I'm a little new at this but it looks like your zsh is finding the epoch time in millis to be too large for an int. Would you mind running this command to verify if that's the case? This looks specific to the zsh port on your device so I don't think I'll be able to reproduce it easily. (Btw, this is a long-shot but just curious if that's the case).\r\n\r\n###### Code: `for i in {30..64}; do ((X=2**$i)); echo \"$i: $X\"; done;`\r\n\r\n###### Sample Output\r\n```\r\n~ ❯ for i in {30..64}; do ((X=2**$i)); echo \"$i: $X\"; done;\r\n30: 1073741824\r\n31: 2147483648\r\n32: 4294967296\r\n33: 8589934592\r\n34: 17179869184\r\n35: 34359738368\r\n36: 68719476736\r\n37: 137438953472\r\n38: 274877906944\r\n39: 549755813888\r\n40: 1099511627776\r\n41: 2199023255552\r\n42: 4398046511104\r\n43: 8796093022208\r\n44: 17592186044416\r\n45: 35184372088832\r\n46: 70368744177664\r\n47: 140737488355328\r\n48: 281474976710656\r\n49: 562949953421312\r\n50: 1125899906842624\r\n51: 2251799813685248\r\n52: 4503599627370496\r\n53: 9007199254740992\r\n54: 18014398509481984\r\n55: 36028797018963968\r\n56: 72057594037927936\r\n57: 144115188075855872\r\n58: 288230376151711744\r\n59: 576460752303423488\r\n60: 1152921504606846976\r\n61: 2305843009213693952\r\n62: 4611686018427387904\r\n63: -9223372036854775808\r\n64: 0\r\n```\r\n\r\n ",
