    "body": "Haha, no worries and thanks for reporting back! I was actually out of ideas after seeing your initial reply 😅\r\nIt looks like the zsh running on your phone uses 32 bits for storing numbers rather than the standard 64. As a long-term thought, you might want to reach out to the zsh owner to fix this.\r\n\r\nThe only workaround I can think of is for us to work with the timestamp as a string rather than int (and lose zsh number-handling features) or count time elapsed against s custom event more recent than the epoch. (which might be confusing but lets us still use zsh's number-handling features). An opinion (or better option) from the maintainers would be good here. Astronauts, any thoughts? (I personally prefer #2 here).\r\n\r\n@alephalpha0, would you mind running the following commands as well just for testing?\r\n\r\n```\r\n((STARSHIP_CAPTURED_TIME = int(rint($EPOCHREALTIME * 1000)))) && echo $STARSHIP_CAPTURED_TIME;\r\necho $EPOCHREALTIME;\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n",
